const BRIEF = `You are implementing three agreed fixes in the repo at /Users/sofianebebert/workspace/sof-pi (a pi package with an extension at extensions/factory/ that runs a pipeline via the installed pi-subagents 0.79.1 and renders a live swimlane waterfall widget). Work only in this repo. Do NOT commit or push — the parent reviews and commits.

Read extensions/factory/index.ts, extensions/factory/src/waterfall.ts, extensions/factory/src/state.ts, extensions/factory/src/rpc.ts, and tests/factory/waterfall.test.ts first. Match existing code style (tabs, fail-closed bounded validation, pure functions in src/waterfall.ts).

## Fix 1 — status token mismatch (lane end times never set)
In extensions/factory/src/waterfall.ts, function laneStateFromStatuses (~line 204) only treats "complete"/"stopped" as finished, but pi-subagents live workflow status emits "completed" (see ~/.pi/agent/npm/node_modules/pi-subagents/src/shared/types.d.ts WorkflowNodeStatus and src/runs/foreground/subagent-executor.js step.status writes). Result: successful lanes never close (endMs stays null) and are force-stamped with the failure instant by closeAllOpenSpans in index.ts:507.
- Accept "completed" as finished everywhere "complete" is accepted (keep accepting "complete" for compatibility).
- Decide and document handling for other WorkflowNodeStatus values ("detached", "rejected", "partial"): map them to a safe lane state (e.g. attention/failed) rather than falling through to "queued". Keep it simple and defensible.
- Update tests/factory/waterfall.test.ts which encodes the wrong token ("complete" at ~lines 155,161,170-173): add a regression test feeding a realistic 'Workflow child <key>: ... completed' status line through parseWorkflowChildStatuses + laneStateFromStatuses and asserting the lane closes (terminal state, not queued).

## Fix 2 — reconcile restored state with real run status (UX dead after resume)
The pipeline advances ONLY on the one-shot subagent:async-complete event (index.ts:659). restore() (index.ts:~278-292) never queries run status; the 3s poll is display-only. If the completion event is lost (e.g. new-process resume — completion ownership is per-process, see pi-subagents src/shared/completion-owner.js and src/runs/background/result-watcher.js:217-233), a restored active phase polls forever, frozen.
- After restore in the session_start and session_tree handlers (index.ts:~691-706), if the restored phase is active (ACTIVE_PHASES) and the relevant run id exists (state.buildRunId when phase build; state.reviewRunId when review), fire ONE one-shot status RPC (reuse rpcRequest pattern from pollOnce). Inspect the returned text for the run's terminal state (e.g. 'State: failed|stopped|complete' — check real format in pi-subagents src/runs/background/run-status.js).
- If terminal: advance to a terminal state idempotently — set state.phase to "failed" (or "needs_attention"), write a clear state.error like 'run reached terminal state (<state>) while this session was away; completion event was not delivered.', closeAllOpenSpans with the matching final state, stopPolling(), save(), updateStatus, and ctx.ui.notify. You cannot reconstruct the full completion payload from status text alone — do not fake a handoff; a clear terminal failure with guidance to rerun /factory is correct.
- If still running: keep the normal poll going (it already does).
- Guard against double-processing: if the real async-complete event also arrives, existing handlers run; make reconcile not race (e.g. skip reconcile if phase already terminal; it is fine if a real completion event lands first since handlers set phase non-active). Add a small once-per-restore flag so session_tree + session_start do not double-fire.
- Handle RPC errors quietly (log/notify minimally; the poll continues).
- Add a test in tests/factory/ (new or existing file) covering the reconcile decision logic. If the logic is embedded in index.ts closure code, extract the pure decision part (e.g. parse run terminal state from status text → 'terminal' | 'running' | 'unknown') into src/ and test that.

## Fix 3 — capture fuller failure diagnostics
The build/review failure branches (index.ts:~503-513 and the review equivalent) set state.error from payload.summary truncated by boundedSummary to 300 chars, and state.error is bounded to 200 chars in isFactoryRunState (state.ts). The truncation hid the actual 'Acceptance rejected: Failed to p...' diagnostic.
- Widen the persisted error bound (e.g. 2000 chars) in state.ts isFactoryRunState and the writer side.
- In the failure branches, include the fullest useful diagnostic available on the payload (summary plus any error/errorTail/message fields present) up to the new bound, keeping the existing message prefix format.
- Ensure formatState still renders it acceptably (it already prints state.error).
- Extend the state restore test to cover a long error surviving round-trip.

## Validation
Run: npm test (from repo root; it runs node --experimental-strip-types --test tests/factory/*.test.ts tests/perplexity/*.test.ts). All must pass. Do not weaken existing assertions.

## Docs (required by AGENTS.md)
Update extensions/factory/README.md (and the factory paragraph in the root README.md if user-visible behavior changed): describe the completed-token handling, the restore-time reconciliation, and the fuller failure diagnostics. Keep edits tight.

## Deliverable
Write a concise report as your final output: files changed with line ranges, decisions taken (esp. detached/rejected/partial mapping and reconcile semantics), test results (pass counts), and any gaps.`;

const impl = await runs.run("implement", {
  agent: "worker",
  context: "fresh",
  task: BRIEF,
});

await state.set("phase", "review");
const review = await runs.run("review", {
  agent: "reviewer",
  context: "fresh",
  task: `Review the uncommitted working-tree changes in /Users/sofianebebert/workspace/sof-pi (git diff). They implement three factory fixes: (1) laneStateFromStatuses must treat "completed" as terminal plus sane handling of detached/rejected/partial, with regression tests; (2) session_start/session_tree must reconcile a restored active factory phase against the real run status via a one-shot status RPC, terminating cleanly when the run finished while away, idempotent, with tests; (3) failure diagnostics: state.error bound widened (~2000) and failure branches persist fuller payload diagnostics, with round-trip test. Check correctness against these requirements, look for regressions (existing tests weakened, race between reconcile and the async-complete event handler, double terminal notifications, restore validation gaps), and run 'npm test' yourself. Return a verdict (ok / fix) with concrete findings: file:line, severity, and whether the implementation matches the brief. Do not edit files.`,
});

return {
  impl: {
    runId: impl.runId,
    ok: impl.ok,
    report: typeof impl.output === "string" ? impl.output.slice(0, 8000) : impl.output,
  },
  review: {
    runId: review.runId,
    ok: review.ok,
    report: typeof review.output === "string" ? review.output.slice(0, 8000) : review.output,
  },
};

